# Copy to .env (git-ignored) and set what you need. Every panini-dr command
# (run, prepare, score, verify) and the scripts under datasets/ read ./.env (or
# the nearest .env in a parent directory) by themselves; variables already set
# in the shell win.
#
# Optional lines are commented out: uncomment a line only when you give it a
# value. An empty value (`NAME=`) is ignored and never sets a variable.

# --- LLM (all roles) -------------------------------------------------------
# OpenAI-compatible base URL of the served model (serve/gpt_oss_120b.sh prints
# it; this is its default). Required by `panini-dr run`.
PANINI_LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/v1
# Served model name. Default: openai/gpt-oss-120b (configs/paper.json).
# PANINI_LLM_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
# Only if your endpoint needs a key (vLLM without --api-key does not; a
# placeholder is sent then). OPENAI_API_KEY is never sent to the LLM endpoint.
# PANINI_LLM_API_KEY=

# --- Retrieval --------------------------------------------------------------
# jina-reranker-v3.5 endpoint (serve/jina_reranker.sh prints it; this is its
# default). Required for the paper configuration.
JINA_RERANK_URL=http://localhost:8090/v1/rerank
# Abort on the first reranker failure (same as --strict-rerank).
# PANINI_STRICT_RERANK=1
# Hugging Face cache for Qwen3-Embedding-8B / reranker weights (default
# ~/.cache/huggingface).
# HF_HOME=/path/to/hf-cache
# Never contact the Hugging Face Hub (set once the weights are downloaded).
# HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1
# Hugging Face token for the gated MoNaCo downloads (or run `hf auth login`).
# HF_TOKEN=
# BrowseComp-Plus Lucene index (pyserini): a full JDK 21.
# JAVA_HOME=/usr/lib/jvm/java-21-openjdk-amd64
# Performance knobs: run the exhaustive dense search on a second GPU / cap the
# FAISS OpenMP threads. Unset in the paper's runs: leave them commented to run
# exactly as those did.
# GSW_DENSE_GPU=cuda:1
# GSW_FAISS_THREADS=16

# --- Data -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Root for prepared datasets and dense caches. Default: ./data
# PANINI_DATA_DIR=/path/to/data
# Override the question files (defaults under PANINI_DATA_DIR).
# MONACO_QUESTIONS=/path/to/monaco_full1315.json
# BROWSECOMP_QUESTIONS=/path/to/browsecomp_plus_830.json

# --- Graders (panini-dr score) ----------------------------------------------
# Judge model name (same as --model; there is no default). It is part of every
# judge-cache key.
# PANINI_JUDGE_MODEL=
# OpenAI-compatible judge endpoint and key, for `--backend openai` (fall back to
# OPENAI_BASE_URL / OPENAI_API_KEY).
# PANINI_JUDGE_BASE_URL=
# PANINI_JUDGE_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# `--backend bedrock` (the default of `panini-dr score answers`): the AWS
# Bedrock region that serves your judge model (falls back to AWS_REGION). AWS
# credentials come from the usual AWS chain.
# PANINI_BEDROCK_REGION=
# AWS_REGION=
# Checkouts of the benchmark authors' grading code, cloned by
# scripts/fetch_grader_sources.py. BCP_REPO (texttron/BrowseComp-Plus) is needed
# to grade short answers (BrowseComp-Plus, FRAMES, your own `short` questions)
# and for BrowseComp-Plus Obs.; MONACO_JUDGE_DIR (the MoNaCo repository) to grade
# set answers (MoNaCo, your own `set` questions).
# BCP_REPO=third_party/BrowseComp-Plus
# MONACO_JUDGE_DIR=third_party/monaco

# Behaviour-changing switches of the research code. They were UNSET in the
# paper runs; `panini-dr run` refuses to start when one is set unless
# --allow-config-drift: GSW_PLANNER_TARGET_HUB_MODE, GSW_STRICT_TARGET_HUB_GATE.
# Variables that only switched code removed from this repository
# (configs/removed_features.json, e.g. GSW_READ_TITLE_FALLBACK) are refused
# outright.
